Spec: Android host

Platform: Kotlin/Gradle

Purpose:
  Android host app: manifest permissions and service, the audio ringer channel and release signing.

Owns:
  ./app
  ./build.gradle.kts
  ./settings.gradle.kts
  ./gradle.properties
  ./gradle
  ./gradlew
  ./gradlew.bat

References:
  /docs/specs/history/05b-gps-platform.md
  /docs/specs/history/21-countdown-cue.md
  /docs/android-release.md

Must:
  `applicationId` is `io.github.valijuu.retrail`; debug builds add `.debug` and the label `Retrail Debug`.
  The `namespace` and Kotlin package stay `com.retrail.retrail`.
  Release builds are signed with the upload key from `key.properties`, and with the debug key when it is missing.
  The recording service is a `location` foreground service on a silent default-importance channel.
  `retrail/audio` answers `isRingerNormal`.
  A new permission is declared on Play (Data safety or foreground-service form) before it ships.

Must not:
  Commit `key.properties` or a keystore.
